  <prompt>Apply auth-v4 integration punch row **A42** — reconcile task 130's C# FIC creation path (`GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic`) with master `Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 -FicOnly` per FR-C4 (don't ship two divergent FIC estates). Choose one of two paths at Step 3 and document the choice: **(a)** H3EntraAppRegHandler DELEGATES to `.\Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 -FicOnly -FederatedCredentialAppId <id> -UamiResourceId <ARM resource ID — NEVER a name; 5 UAMIs exist in dev, `spaarke-bff-identity` is a decoy> -TenantId <tenant>` as a **subprocess (NEVER dot-source — dot-source pollutes runtime session state)**, captures exit code + parses structured output; OR **(b)** keep both implementations under ONE written contract in `notes/decisions/` with **parity tests** asserting: idempotency by (issuer,subject,audience) triple; propagation retry on `AADSTS70025` (measured code — **NOT** 70021; retry MUST exact-match numeric `error_codes` because substring matchers also catch 700211/700213 which are genuine config faults); exit codes 0/1/2 semantics (0 = created+verified; 1 = created but verify failed; 2 = structurally-correct-unverifiable = NORMAL off-Azure — REQUIRES a recorded post-App-Service verification, NEVER terminal success). Under BOTH paths: **port master's `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy` cross-tenant refusal guard** (verified present on master; verified ABSENT from the C# provisioner — SF-5) into `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic`. E2E closes auth-v4 §11 invariants 1+2 (wrong-subject → `AADSTS700213` detected; fresh-FIC flap ~8 failures/~130s retried) — first real exercise on r1. Model 1 (I6): zero FIC calls — task-130 I6 tests assert `ProvisionCallCount==0`; MUST NOT regress. Publish-size: A42 does NOT touch BFF (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**`) — NFR-01 verification N/A per root CLAUDE.md §10. Amend punch list annotations. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE L2 control-plane handler author + Azure Federated Identity Credential (FIC) contract expert + PowerShell subprocess-invocation hardening specialist. Expert in: `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic` current behavior (per-profile issuer at `:547-557`, `customer-owned-model2` → customer tenant, else Spaarke tenant; reading-(a)-consistent per remediation plan §3.2); master `Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 -FicOnly` contract (16 occurrences on master, exit codes 0/1/2, triple-keyed idempotency, `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy` cross-tenant refusal, `AADSTS70025` exact-match retry with ~8 failures/~130s propagation flap window); FIC object shape recipe (issuer/subject-as-principalId-NOT-clientId/audience — auth-v4 §3.1); the 5-UAMI decoy trap (SF-1: ARM resource IDs only, `spaarke-bff-identity` is NOT the BFF UAMI); task-130 I6 test contract (Model 1 → `ProvisionCallCount==0`, 2 dedicated tests); auth-v4 §11 live invariants (1 = wrong-subject → `AADSTS700213`; 2 = fresh-FIC flap retry); §9.2 escalation gate (customer-owned Model 2 blocked pending Q2 ratification — task 186 profile `spaarke-hosted-model2` is UNAFFECTED per Q9 verification 2026-08-25).</role>

  <goal>H3EntraAppRegHandler + GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner reconciled per FR-C4 — one of: **(a)** H3 subprocess-delegates to `Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 -FicOnly` with exit-code capture + structured-output parsing + PS script contract documented in code comments; **(b)** dual C#+PS implementations retained under ONE named-contract document in `notes/decisions/205b-a42-fic-parity-contract.md` PLUS a parity test suite running BOTH implementations against the same fixtures. `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy` equivalent PORTED into `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic` (cross-tenant refusal guard active — refuses when app-reg tenant ≠ UAMI tenant with loud provisioning-time failure). Unit + integration tests assert: (a) idempotency by triple `(issuer, subject, audience)` — name-only check MUST fail the test; (b) `AADSTS70025` propagation retry EXACT-MATCH (a fixture emitting `700211` or `700213` MUST NOT trigger retry — must fail-fast as genuine config fault); (c) exit code 0/1/2 semantics honored — 2 is NOT terminal success; (d) every exit-2 outcome records a `PendingPostAppServiceVerification=true` marker in `ProvisioningRun` state; (e) I6 Model 1 `ProvisionCallCount==0` assertions PRESERVED (existing task-130 tests still green); (f) cross-tenant refusal fires on wrong tenancy (test injects app-reg tenant ≠ UAMI tenant → expects refusal exception, NOT silent create). Auth-v4 §11 invariants 1+2 exercised in acceptance tests. `dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` succeeds. `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core.Tests/` succeeds (all pre-existing tests + new A42 tests). No BFF touch → NFR-01 publish-size verification N/A (state explicitly in task summary).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Auth-v4 §10 DELIVERED (2026-08-21) shipped `-FicOnly` FIC automation in `Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1` on master: exit codes 0/1/2, triple-keyed idempotency, measured `AADSTS70025` propagation retry (NOT the documented 70021 — that code never appeared live), `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy` cross-tenant refusal guard. Independently, r1 task 130 landed a C# FIC creation path in `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic` — the §9.3-anticipated fallback path. Both now exist. Auth-v4 §9.3's timing caveat pre-authorized this ("if task 130 lands first, r1 owes a reconciliation"). FR-C4 (§4 of the remediation plan): don't leave two divergent FIC estates diverging silently — the exact class of failure SF-4 warns against (L2 cannot exchange-verify FIC it creates; verification degrades to re-GET byte-compare against `request.UamiPrincipalId`). Verified 2026-08-25: master's `Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1` contains `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy` (2 occurrences); THIS branch's `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs` does NOT — cross-tenant refusal is a total gap (SF-5). §5.1 DECIDED (owner 2026-08-25): Reading 1 for Model 1 (one shared multitenant app-reg; zero per-customer app-reg/FIC objects for Model 1 — I6 `ProvisionCallCount==0`). §9.2 OPEN (Q2 pending): customer-owned Model 2 stamp tenancy — reading (a) same-tenant FIC (structurally supported; shipped code implements this at `:547-557`) vs reading (b) cross-tenant FIC (unsupported by Entra's same-tenant FIC rule; would require KV certificate fallback per A4). Q9 CONFIRMED 2026-08-25 via remediation plan §7 dependency register: task 186 targets `spaarke-hosted-model2` profile (POML line 20 + 60 verified) → intra-tenant Spaarke-hosted → §9.2 does NOT affect 186. §11 live-test invariants 1+2 handed to Wave G-3 for first real exercise: (1) wrong-subject `AADSTS700213` detection; (2) fresh-FIC flap ~8 failures over ~130s retried. A42 delivers that exercise. **This task does NOT touch BFF** — landing spots are all under `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/**` (L2 control-plane) + tests. NFR-01 publish-size verification per root CLAUDE.md §10 is N/A; state explicitly to prevent reviewer confusion.</background>
