  <constraints>
    <constraint source="A42 row spec (draft-punch-rows.md) + FR-C4">MUST NOT ship two divergent FIC estates unchecked. Choose path (a) subprocess delegation OR path (b) parity-tested dual path — the choice + rationale MUST be documented in either the code comments (path a) or a `notes/decisions/205b-a42-fic-parity-contract.md` document (path b).</constraint>
    <constraint source="A42 row spec — dot-source ban">If path (a) chosen: MUST invoke `Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 -FicOnly` as a **SUBPROCESS** (`System.Diagnostics.Process` / `pwsh -File`). MUST NOT dot-source (`. .\Register-...`). Dot-source pollutes runtime session state with the script's functions + variables — breaks isolation and repeat-invocation correctness.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §10 DELIVERED + code-review C1 (SF-6)">MUST exact-match numeric `error_codes` array on `AADSTS70025` propagation retry. MUST NOT substring-match `70025` — substring matchers also catch `700211` (wrong issuer) and `700213` (wrong subject) which are genuine config faults, NOT propagation delays; substring retry burns the full retry budget then asserts the OPPOSITE verdict.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §10 DELIVERED + SF-8">MUST honor exit codes 0/1/2 semantics: 0 = created+verified end-to-end; 1 = created but verification failed (a real failure); 2 = structurally-correct-but-unverifiable-from-this-host = the NORMAL off-Azure result when the invoker cannot mint an assertion for the created FIC. Treating exit-2 as failure breaks legitimate runs; treating it as terminal success SHIPS AN UNVERIFIED FIC.</constraint>
    <constraint source="SF-8 + remediation plan §5 item 2">MUST record a `PendingPostAppServiceVerification=true` marker in `ProvisioningRun` state on every exit-2 outcome, deferring true exchange-verification to post-App-Service (H13/T4). Exit-2 is NEVER terminal success in the run report.</constraint>
    <constraint source="SF-5 + A42 row spec + auth-v4 script `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy`">MUST port the cross-tenant tenancy refusal guard (`Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy`) into `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic`. Verified present on master's PS script (2 occurrences); verified ABSENT from the C# provisioner. Under reading (a) the guard is inert protection; under reading (b) it converts silent production failure (weeks later at first OBO) into loud provisioning-time refusal. Guard fires when app-reg tenant ≠ UAMI tenant.</constraint>
    <constraint source="SF-1 + A42 row spec">MUST use ARM resource IDs for UAMI (full `/subscriptions/.../providers/Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities/{name}` shape). MUST NOT resolve UAMI by name — 5 UAMIs exist in the dev subscription; `spaarke-bff-identity` is a DECOY not attached to the BFF (SF-1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="SF-7 + auth-v4 §3.1">MUST preserve FIC idempotency by the (issuer, subject, audience) triple. MUST NOT idempotency-check by FIC name alone. Entra enforces the triple per application; a name-only check turns a correct no-op into a failed run (auth-v4 hit this live on the first run).</constraint>
    <constraint source="task-130 landed + spec.md FR-40 (I6) + Model 1 tenancy">MUST NOT regress task-130's I6 Model 1 assertions (`ProvisionCallCount==0` — 2 dedicated tests). Model 1 flow makes ZERO FIC calls; A42 reconciliation MUST NOT introduce a code path that fires FIC creation under Model 1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Q2 (§9.2) escalation-gate — remediation plan §7 dependency register">If a customer-owned-tenant Model 2 dispatch is attempted while §9.2 (Q2) remains unratified, STOP per root CLAUDE.md §6 (auth-sensitive). Task 186 uses `spaarke-hosted-model2` (Q9 verified) → intra-tenant → SAFE. Any acceptance test fixture using profile `customer-owned-model2` requires Q2 disposition first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 BFF Hygiene NFR-01">A42 does NOT touch `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**`. Publish-size verification is N/A. State explicitly in task summary to prevent reviewer confusion (a BFF-touching task summary omitting the number is a §10 violation; a non-BFF-touching task must SAY so).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 component justification (three-question template)">If path (b) chosen: `notes/decisions/205b-a42-fic-parity-contract.md` is a NEW file → MUST cite A42 in header + answer Existing/Extension/Cost-of-doing-nothing (see `<notes>` §11 justification below for the pattern).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §8.5 TEST-MODIFYING override + auth tag">Adds/modifies tests under `tests/unit/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core.Tests/**` → code-review + adr-check run UNCONDITIONALLY at Step 9.5 (not skipped). Auth tag confirms.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md ADR-028 A4 (post-A35)">FIC subject MUST be UAMI `principalId` (NOT `clientId`). Verified §3.1 recipe; wrong-subject → `AADSTS700213` (§11 invariant 1). Preserve throughout A42 changes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

