  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL, xhigh effort, model-tier=fable). Read A42 row verbatim from `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`. Read remediation plan §4 (delta impact) + §5 items 1-4 (silent-failure priority surfaces) + §7 (sequencing + dependency register) + §8 (effort/cost). Read `decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` (§6.5 record — cite it wherever the FIC subprocess touches secret-free-env assumptions). Read `.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md` (verify A4 + E-3 CLOSED banner present post-A35 merge). Read `.claude/constraints/auth.md` (verify :108 corrected post-A35). Read `H3EntraAppRegHandler.cs` (current script-invocation seam or lack thereof) + `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs` (verify `:547-557` per-profile issuer + `:73-78` header recipe still present).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep-verify current state BEFORE applying">Run: (a) `grep -n "Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy" scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1` — MUST return ≥2 matches (verifies A35 landed the guard). (b) `grep -n "Assert.*Tenancy\|CrossTenant\|ValidateTenancy" src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs` — MUST return 0 matches (verifies SF-5 gap still present; if it returns matches, ANOTHER agent already ported it — inspect + reconcile before proceeding). (c) `grep -n "FicOnly\|-FicOnly" scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1` — MUST return ≥16 matches (A35 sanity). (d) `grep -n "AADSTS70025\|70021" src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/**/*.cs` — record current retry-code state. (e) `grep -n "ProvisionCallCount" tests/**/*.cs` — record I6 test signatures for regression check. Record verified state in scratchpad table BEFORE any edit.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Read task-130 landed tests + I6 contract">Read `tests/unit/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core.Tests/Handlers/EntraAppReg/**` (or the equivalent path — task-130 lands here). Document the EXACT assertions I6 Model 1 tests make on `ProvisionCallCount==0`. Any change in `CreateFic` MUST leave these tests green. Note fixture patterns for reuse in new A42 tests.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Path decision — (a) subprocess delegation vs (b) parity dual-path">Evaluate against: (i) maintenance cost of two implementations vs (ii) subprocess-invocation fragility (pwsh availability in L2 worker container, exit-code portability across script versions, structured-output parsing surface). RECOMMENDED default: **path (a)** — one authoritative implementation (master PS `-FicOnly`) reduces divergence surface + auth-v4 owns its script contract. Path (b) chosen ONLY if subprocess invocation is architecturally incompatible with L2 worker runtime (verify: does the L2 worker container have `pwsh` in PATH?). Document decision + rationale in code header comments (path a) or `notes/decisions/205b-a42-fic-parity-contract.md` (path b) with §11 three-question justification.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Checkpoint (after grep + read + decision)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "✅ Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="5" name="Port Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy into GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic (BOTH paths)">Read master PS `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy` function body verbatim. Port its semantics into a C# method `AssertFicTenancy(appRegTenantId, uamiTenantId, profile)` in `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner`. Throw a distinct exception type (e.g., `CrossTenantFicRefusedException`) — NOT a generic `InvalidOperationException`. Call it FIRST in `CreateFic` before any Graph API call. Guard fires when `appRegTenantId != uamiTenantId` and `profile != "customer-owned-model2"` — under reading (a) profile `customer-owned-model2` legitimately has same-tenant FIC (customer tenant hosts both app-reg AND stamp UAMI); under reading (b) the guard MUST refuse loudly. Add code comment citing SF-5 + §9.2 + `decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` §9.2 contingency.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Path (a) apply — H3 subprocess delegation + exit-code capture">IF path (a) chosen: EDIT `H3EntraAppRegHandler` to invoke `pwsh -File .\Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 -FicOnly -FederatedCredentialAppId <appRegId> -UamiResourceId <ARM resource ID — full /subscriptions/.../userAssignedIdentities/{name} shape, SF-1> -TenantId <resolved tenant>` via `System.Diagnostics.Process` (NEVER `Runspace` dot-source). Capture stdout + stderr + exit code. Map exit codes: 0 → success + FIC verified; 1 → failure (throw); 2 → success + `PendingPostAppServiceVerification=true` marker written to `ProvisioningRun` state. Parse structured output (JSON block written by `-FicOnly`) for the created FIC's `(issuer,subject,audience)` triple + persist to inter-step state. Retry on `AADSTS70025` exact-match (from stderr parse) — up to 8 attempts / ~130s per §11 invariant 2. Delegate cross-tenant refusal to Step 5's C# guard (fired BEFORE subprocess invocation, not delegated to PS — belt + suspenders because the L2 worker holds the tenancy metadata natively).</step>
    <step order="6b" name="Path (b) apply — parity contract + dual-implementation">IF path (b) chosen: Author `notes/decisions/205b-a42-fic-parity-contract.md` documenting: (i) canonical FIC-creation contract (issuer/subject/audience recipe, idempotency triple, retry codes, exit-code semantics, cross-tenant refusal); (ii) parity test suite design (both C# `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic` and PS `-FicOnly` MUST behave identically against the same fixture set); (iii) maintenance obligation (any change to one MUST be mirrored in the other + parity tests re-run); (iv) §11 three-question justification. Keep `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic` as-is functionally (task-130 landed) BUT: add `AssertFicTenancy` (Step 5), fix retry to exact-match `AADSTS70025` (not substring, not 70021), add exit-code equivalent semantics (return-value enum with `Created`/`CreatedNotVerified`/`CreatedPendingPostAppServiceVerification`), add triple-key idempotency check (not name-only).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Checkpoint (after path apply)">Run `context-handoff`.</step>
