  <notes>
Justification (root CLAUDE.md §11 three-question template):

**Existing** — Two FIC-creation surfaces exist as of 2026-08-25: (1) master's `Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 -FicOnly` (16 occurrences on master; shipped by auth-v4 §10 DELIVERED 2026-08-21 with exit codes 0/1/2, triple-keyed idempotency, `AADSTS70025` exact-match retry, `Assert-SpaarkeFicTenancy` cross-tenant refusal); (2) r1 task 130's `GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic` in C# (per-profile issuer at `:547-557`, reading-(a)-consistent, but MISSING the cross-tenant refusal guard — SF-5). Auth-v4 §9.3 pre-authorized the r1 fallback path AND requested reconciliation via FR-C4. A42 exists BECAUSE the fallback fired.

**Extension** — This task does NOT introduce a NEW FIC-creation surface. It RECONCILES the two existing surfaces into one authoritative path — either (a) path-(a) subprocess delegation (H3 → PS `-FicOnly` — one implementation authoritative) OR (b) path-(b) parity-tested dual implementations under one named contract. Under path (b), the ONE new file (`notes/decisions/205b-a42-fic-parity-contract.md`) is a decision record, not a component. `AssertFicTenancy` and `CrossTenantFicRefusedException` are the only new symbols; both are ports of existing PS-script semantics into C#, not new abstractions — they close SF-5, they don't introduce a layer.

**Cost of doing nothing** — Three concrete failure modes ship with the current two-divergent-estates state: (1) any provisioning run picking the C# path (`GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.CreateFic`) silently creates cross-tenant FIC pairs on customer-owned Model 2 stamps because the tenancy refusal guard is absent (SF-5) — failure surfaces WEEKS LATER at the customer's first OBO call as `AADSTS700213`, in production, on a customer sub, with no provisioning-time signal; (2) the two paths diverge over time without parity enforcement — a future retry-code change to the PS script (say `AADSTS70025` → `AADSTS70025|AADSTS70023` for a new propagation code) never lands in C#, and half the fleet retries correctly while the other half fails after budget-burn to the OPPOSITE verdict; (3) `-FicOnly` exit-code semantics (0/1/2) are undefined in the C# path — any code path treating C# `CreateFic`'s return as terminal success on the off-Azure equivalent of exit-2 ships an UNVERIFIED FIC, blocking `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` at first BFF boot with an opaque `AADSTS7000215` and no diagnostic trail. A42 exists to prevent all three by making the two estates converge on ONE contract. FR-C4 is the binding rule; SF-5, SF-6, SF-7, SF-8 are the specific silent-failure surfaces this row closes.

**Cross-references**: Row A42 in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`. Remediation plan §4 delta impact + §5 items 1-4 + §7 dependency register + §8 cost posture. Q2 (§9.2) escalation-gate per remediation plan §7 (customer-owned Model 2 blocked pending Q2; Q9 confirms task 186 UNAFFECTED). §6.5 resolution record `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` (A4/E-3 closure — cite where CreateFic touches secret-free-env assumptions).

**NFR-01 note**: A42 does NOT touch `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**` — the H3 handler + FIC provisioner live under `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/` (L2 control-plane). Publish-size verification per root CLAUDE.md §10 is N/A; state explicitly in task summary.
  </notes>

